        "title": "Differentiating a Quotient Containing Other Functions"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "c6dfc180-f423-59a1-98b7-de10e7a93f4f",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Given $f(x)=\\frac{e^{x}}{2}$ and $h(x)=- 4 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}$, calculate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h})$.\n\n| $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h})=$ | $\\frac{e^{x}}{8}($ {{field-1}} $)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | $\\sin^2 x$ |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\sin(x).$\n\nWe apply the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h})&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(\\frac{e^{x}}{2})^{\\prime}\\cdot (- 4 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})-(\\frac{e^{x}}{2})\\cdot (- 4 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(- 4 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\sin(x))-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\cos(x))}{16\\sin^{2}(x)}\\\\ &=\\frac{2{e}^{x}(\\cos(x)-\\sin(x))}{16\\sin^{2}(x)}\\\\ &=\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\cos(x)-\\sin(x))}{8\\sin^{2}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "b79a16cf-1ff2-540f-afa8-69dbee7e850e",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
